Pinned-source audit:
- Mapped all six public `DefaultMQProducer.request` overloads, request preparation, correlation UUID generation, request holder/future lifecycle, reply helper, reply header, and inbound reply processor into `docs/compatibility/PHASE_15_REQUEST_REPLY_MATRIX.md`.
- Confirmed Java uses `UUID.randomUUID().toString()`, writes `CORRELATION_ID`, `REPLY_TO_CLIENT`, and decimal `TTL`, includes route/heartbeat preparation in the original request timeout, and sends with async-mode retry behavior.
- Confirmed the Java singleton scans at 3s initial delay / 1s period, and atomically removes expired/replied entries before one callback. Reply helper requires request + `CLUSTER`, sets `<cluster>_REPLY_TOPIC`, `MSG_TYPE=reply`, correlation/reply-to/TTL. Reply processor returns SUCCESS for unknown/late/duplicate IDs and SYSTEM_ERROR on receive/decode failures.
- Baseline implementation has reply request codes and typed headers, plus an inbound routing slot. It lacks request API, pending correlation storage, reply helper and completion dispatcher; unknown correlation currently yields REQUEST_CODE_NOT_SUPPORTED.

Phase 15 implementation and verification are in progress; no completion claims yet.

